"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every pair’s minimum cut value is the least capacity on its tree path, and every tree edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"splits the vertices into a minimum cut between its ends. Computed by Gusfield’s algorithm"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the canonical cut, vertices in order, rooted at the first: n − 1 maximum flows on one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"residual network, by push–relabel’s first phase. Disconnected graphs get zero-capacity tree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges. "},{"code":"capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is called once per non-loop edge, in position order, before any work."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The flows run in a wider type than "},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" where needed ("},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"Int128","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for fixed-width"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"integers, "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"code":"Float","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), so a vertex’s capacity sum may exceed "},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s range."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every capacity is at least zero, not NaN and finite, and every tree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"capacity (a minimum cut value) fits in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"name":"Precondition","type":"aside"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"A Gomory–Hu cut tree, or nil for the empty graph.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"Flows","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"